Cybersecurity Risk Matrix
Purpose
This risk matrix prioritizes cybersecurity risks identified during the simulated small-business assessment.
Risks are evaluated based on their potential impact to the organization and the likelihood that the risk could occur.
Risk Ratings
Risk	Likelihood	Impact	Overall Priority
No multi factor authentication	High	High	Critical
Shared or reused passwords	High	High	Critical
Excessive user permissions	Medium	High	High
Lack of tested backups	Medium	High	High
Phishing attacks	High	Medium	High
Inactive accounts not removed	Medium	Medium	Medium
Lack of security awareness training	Medium	Medium	Medium
Risk Prioritization
Critical
Multi factor authentication
Accounts without MFA are at increased risk if credentials are compromised. Critical business accounts should have MFA enabled as a priority.
Shared or Reused Passwords
Shared or reused credentials make it more difficult to identify account activity and increase the potential impact of a compromised password.
High
Excessive User Permissions
Users should only have access necessary to perform their responsibilities.
Lack of Tested Backups
Backups should be maintained and periodically tested to ensure that important information can be recovered.
Phishing attacks
Phishing can result in stolen credentials, malware infections, financial fraud, or unauthorized access.
Medium
Inactive accounts
Accounts belonging to former employees or inactive users should be disabled or removed promptly.
Lack of Security Awareness Training
Employees should receive basic training on phishing, passwords, MFA, suspicious messages, and security reporting procedures.
Recommended Order of Action
Enable MFA on critical accounts.
Eliminate shared and reused passwords.
Review administrator and user permissions.
Establish and test a reliable backup process.
Implement phishing awareness training.
Establish an employee account offboarding process.
Review security controls periodically.
Conclusion
Risk prioritization allows a small organization to focus limited time and resources on the cybersecurity issues that could have the greatest impact.
The highest priority recommendations in this assessment focus on account security, access control, and data recovery.
